# CareBridge AI rules

## Product

CareBridge AI is a hackathon prototype for care continuity between patients and authorized doctors.

## Technology

Use:
- React
- Vite
- JavaScript
- Tailwind CSS
- Recharts
- Local synthetic data first

Do not add Firebase, authentication, or external APIs until the local MVP works.

## Safety

Never:
- Diagnose a patient.
- Prescribe medication.
- Change dosage.
- Recommend stopping medication.
- Claim a symptom confirms a disease.
- Invent patient events.
- Use real patient data.
- Present an AI summary as a clinical decision.

Always:
- Label symptoms as “patient-reported”.
- Label flags as “requires professional review”.
- Preserve original patient notes.
- Show the report date range.
- Show exact underlying activities.
- Include a professional-review disclaimer in reports.

## Workflow

- Read PROJECT_SPEC.md and UX_SPEC.md before implementation.
- Do not change product scope without asking the user.
- Implement one milestone at a time.
- Do not rewrite unrelated working files.
- Before editing, explain which files will change.
- After editing, run the app and check for errors.
- Use mock data until the user explicitly approves a backend.
- Use reusable components.
- Keep patient screens mobile-first.
- Keep doctor screens desktop/tablet-friendly.
- Do not replace working UI with a new design without approval.

## Mode behavior

In Plan mode:
- Do not edit files.
- Do not run commands.
- Only inspect the project and propose a plan.

In Agent mode:
- Implement only the approved milestone.
- Stop after the milestone.
- Report changed files, tests performed, and remaining issues.